    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d427">

                <pb facs="0528" n="1362" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1362"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 659a.119/2</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-06T23:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 6, 1918, 11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 6, 9.45
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8540. War Trade Board [from Sheldon]:</p>
                <p>Restriction of Enemy Supplies Department reminds us that Iceland negotiations are
                    awaiting your reply to our No. 8421. Proposal has been made to Board of Trade to
                    stop dealing in Icelandic produce by private British firms pending negotiations,
                    provided the United States Government agrees to adopt same course. Sheldon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
